          "content": "For 95% of human history, our ancestors were hunter-gatherers. Around 10,000 BCE, the Neolithic Revolution began — humans started farming, settling down, and inventing tools that would multiply human labor a thousandfold. Three inventions defined this age: the wheel, the plow, and irrigation. Together they made cities possible.",
